  "method": "Multi-Criteria Analytical Hierarchy Process (AHP) integrating 8 thematic parameters: DEM-derived geomorphology proxy, auto-extracted lineaments, slope, ISRIC SoilGrids infiltration, D8 drainage density, CHIRPS rainfall, Copernicus Sentinel-1/2 land use, and surface water proximity. Consistency Ratio CR = 0.0292 (passed < 0.10 threshold). Classified with Jenks natural breaks. Artificial recharge sites selected using multi-parameter suitability rules.",
  "limitations": "This is a hydrogeological potential index based on surface and terrain proxies, not in-situ piezometric well levels. Lineaments are auto-extracted via Canny edge detection and filtered against roads. Geomorphology landforms are DEM-derived topographic proxies (TPI/slope), not NRSC ground geomorphology maps. Foothill recharge zones in the Western Ghats are excluded by design to focus on the farmable plains. Geology not included \u2014 GSI lithology pending.",
